hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1252","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya told us, Yazid bin Kaysan told us, Abu Hazim told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We had a wedding with the Messenger of God. We did not wake up until the sun had risen, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let every person take his head. His mount, for this is a place where Satan has come to us.” We neglected it, so he called for water and performed ablution, then he prayed two prostrations, then the prayer was established and he prayed. In the morning. I told this story in another place, during the sleep of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the morning prayer until the sun rose."
"1253","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, my father told us, and Shuaib told us, they said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, On the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Busra Al-Ghafari, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, that he said: I traveled with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Eighteen journeys, and I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, leave two rak’ahs when the sun was setting. I did not see him leave two rak’ahs before \Noon.\"" Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us"," Ibn Wahb told us"," Al-Layth told us"," and Abu Yahya bin Sulayman is Falih"," on the authority of Safwan Ibn Sulaym"," with this chain of transmission"," is similar to it"," except that he said: I did not see him neglecting two rak’ahs before noon."""
"1254","The Kufans narrated a miracle, on the authority of Ibn Omar: I am afraid that it will not be permissible to narrate it unless its cause is made clear, not that it is a miracle in the text. However, it is a marvel in the chain of transmission in this story. They were narrated on the authority of Nafi’ and Attiya bin Saad Al-Awfi, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: “I prayed with The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was present and travelling, so I prayed four rak’ahs during the noon prayer with him, and after that two rak’ahs, and four rak’ahs during the afternoon. There are three rak’ahs after which there are nothing, and Maghrib is three rak’ahs, and after that two rak’ahs, and the evening prayer is four rak’ahs, and after that two rak’ahs, and the morning is two rak’ahs, He prayed two rak'ahs before that, and I prayed with him on the journey, the noon prayer two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs after it, and the afternoon prayer two rak'ahs, and nothing after it. And the Maghrib prayer is three rak’ahs, and after that two rak’ahs.” He said: “It is the odd number of the daytime, not lacking when present or travelling, and the evening prayer is two rak’ahs, and after it Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs in the morning, and two rak'ahs before that.\ Narrated by Abu Al-Khattab"," narrated by Malik bin Sa’ir"," narrated by Ibn Abi Laila"," on the authority of Nafi’"," and Atiya bin Saad Al-Awfi"," on the authority of Ibn Omar. This news was narrated by a group of Kufans"," on the authority of Atiyya"," on the authority of Ibn Umar"," among them Ash’ath ibn Sawwar"," Firas"," and Hajjaj ibn Artat. Some of them summarized the hadith"," and some of them mentioned it in its length. This is news that is not hidden from anyone who knows the hadith"," that this is an error and an oversight on the authority of Ibn Umar. Ibn Umar"," may God have mercy on him"," denied voluntary travel"," and he says: If I had been voluntary"," I would not have bothered to complete the prayer"," and he said: I saw the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," not praying before or after it in Travel"""
"1255","Bundar told us, Yahya told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, Uthman bin Abdullah bin Suraqah told me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “not praying before or after it while traveling.”"
"1256","And Bundar told us, we are Uthman, meaning Ibn Omar, we are Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Uthman Ibn Abdullah Ibn Suraqa, that he saw Hafs bin Asim was swimming on a journey, and with them on that journey was Abdullah bin Omar. It was said: Your uncle forbids this, so I asked Ibn Omar about That, so he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, not doing that. He did not pray before or after the prayer. I said: Should I pray at night? He said: “Pray during the night as much as you wish.”"
"1257","Bundar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Issa bin Hafs, on the authority of Yahya bin Hakim, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Issa bin Hafs means Ibn Asim Ibn Omar Ibn Al-Khattab. Bundar said: My father told me, and Yahya said: My father told me, he said: I was with Ibn Omar in He traveled and prayed two rak'ahs of noon and afternoon prayers, then he went to his prayer room and saw people praising God, meaning praying. He said: \What are these people doing?\"" He said: I said: They praise. He said: “If I had been praying before or after it"," I would have completed it. I would have accompanied the Messenger of God"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," until he died. It was not more than two rak’ahs"," and Abu Bakr"," Omar"," and Othman did the same.” This is the wording of the hadith of Yahya bin Hakim. Abu Bakr said: Ibn Umar"," may God have mercy on him"," denies voluntary travel after the obligatory prayer"," and says: If I had been praising God"," I would have completed the prayer"," so how does he view it? The Prophet"," may God’s prayers and peace be upon him"," performed two voluntary rak’ahs while traveling after the prescribed noon prayer"," then he denounced those who did what the Prophet"," may God’s prayers and peace be upon him"," did. Peace be upon him"," Salem"," and Hafs bin Asim are more knowledgeable about Ibn Umar and have better memory of his hadith than Atiyya bin Saad."""
"1258","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Salim bin Abd told me By God, that Abdullah bin Omar “would not prostrate himself on a journey before or after the obligatory prayers until he got up in the middle of the night, and he would not He abandons standing in the middle of the night.”"
"1259","And Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Yaman told us, Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Asim bin Abdullah told me, Hafs bin Asim bin Omar bin Al-Khattab told him that he asked Abdullah bin Omar about his abandoning the rosary while travelling, so Abdul told him God: “If I had glorified God, I would not have cared to complete the prayer.” Al-Zuhri said: So I said to Salim: Did you ask Abdullah bin Omar about what Hafs asked him about? Bin Asim? Salem said: No, we were afraid of him about some issue. Abu Bakr said: Salem and Hafs reported on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Omar is an illusion. Ibn Abi Laila is an illusion in his combination of Nafi’ and Attiya in the narration of Ibn Omar regarding voluntary travel, except that this is of the type that We say that it is not permissible to use denial as proof against Ibn Umar, may God have mercy on him, even if he did not see the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, volunteering to travel. Others saw him praying voluntarily while travelling, and the ruling is for the one who reports seeing the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, not for the one who did not see him. This may be an issue. I have explained it in more than one place in our books."
